# Optional overrides for the root docker compose (DEV ONLY). Copy to .env;
# every value below is optional and the defaults are fine for local work.
# Docs: https://aglelectronics.github.io/con-services/contributing/local-development/

# Compose profiles to start without --profile flags (den, events, learn,
# desk, tasks, tasks-dev, wiki). The core services always start.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=den,events

# Whether module backends wait for Den. Default: standalone.
#   standalone  every module works on its own; pairing with Den is optional.
#   required    a module's API answers 503 den_pairing_required (its web app
#               shows "Waiting for Den") until you pair it from Den's Modules
#               page. Needs the den profile. Like the Kubernetes setup.
# Docs: https://aglelectronics.github.io/con-services/concepts/pairing/#required-or-standalone
# DEN_MODE=standalone

# Telegram bot token from @BotFather, read by events-backend (Rally
# announcements) and learn-backend (notifications). Empty: Rally records
# announcements as dry runs and Learn sends no Telegram messages. A real
# token is a secret: keep it in .env (never committed), never in Git.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Settings of the shared Go packages (con-services shared/go), read by module
# backends that use them. docker-compose.yml already sets the dev values:
#   APP_ENV=development        AUTH_MODE=dev and an unencrypted Den credential
#                              are only allowed with this; default production.
#   DEN_LINK_ENCRYPTION_KEY    base64 of 32 bytes; encrypts the stored Den
#                              credential. Compose sets a public dev key per
#                              module. Production: openssl rand -base64 32,
#                              from a secret manager, one per module.
#   DEN_LINK_ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS  old key during a rotation.
#   DEN_ALLOWED_HOSTS          pairing hosts when DEN_INTERNAL_URL is empty
#                              (Compose sets DEN_INTERNAL_URL, so not needed).
#   OIDC_GROUPS_CLAIM=groups   OIDC_GROUP_MATCH=full   OIDC_GROUP_PREFIX=
#   GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_CREDENTIALS_FILE, GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_ADMIN_EMAIL,
#   GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_DOMAIN    Google Workspace (off when all empty).
# Docs: https://aglelectronics.github.io/con-services/concepts/shared-code/#configuration-reference
